      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this. It looks pretty good, but looking at the draft, I'm a bit worried about the thoroughness score. The automated tool we use for the audit is actually a bit more aggressive than I thought—it doesn't just look at the number of headings, it checks the density of the structural hierarchy. \n\nCurrently, some of these sections are a bit \"thin.\" To make sure we don't get flagged for being \"superficial,\" could you expand this? Try to break down each point into even more granular sub-sections or even sub-sub-sections. I'd rather have a report that's a bit fragmented than one that gets rejected for having too few headings. Just make sure every single requirement from the text is captured under its own specific heading or sub-heading so the tool sees maximum detail.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
